  "caption": "Quinn hit the boxing bag like it owed rent — no wraps. By week two, wrists, knuckles and shoulders complained.\n\nKay explains that hands, wrists and shoulders take a lot of load in boxing, while head knocks are the serious concern. Fitness boxing without sparring is much lower risk. And a sore knuckle isn't always just bruising.\n\nWhat can help: learn technique before hitting hard, wrap your hands every session, build grip, wrist, shoulder and neck strength, limit sparring and head contact, and increase bag and pad volume gradually.\n\nGet it checked if a concussion is suspected (stop and get assessed), knuckle pain or hand swelling lingers — it may need an X-ray — or wrist pain won't settle.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
